# nr-relay-twin-legs: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Already applied: the suite (tests/twin/scenarios/legs, 35 scenarios) and its ledger.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/twin/normalise.rs (in-crate edit) is NOT applied: exact text
The relay's own log lines of both runtimes differ by nature in: "[relay] phone leg closed client=1a2b3c4d code=1000 reason= lived=5ms" (8 hex of the random phone id, the leg's lifetime) and the 30 s line "[relay] sockets 30s phones=1 buffered desktop:7c1f3a52=0B phone:d8601a87=0B loop-p50=31.6ms loop-p99=32.3ms loop-max=34.2ms" (the desktop:<8 hex> part is fixed by the scenarios and stays; so does device=7c1f3a52 of "phone upgrade refused").
1. struct Normaliser, after the field re_port: Option<Regex>, add:

    re_relay_log: Regex,

2. Normaliser::new, in the Ok(Self { ... }) literal, after re_port, add:

            re_relay_log: regex(r"(client=|phone:)[0-9a-f]{8}\b|(lived=|loop-(?:p50|p99|max)=)\d+(?:\.\d+)?ms")?,

3. Normaliser::string, replace the line "        text = self.identifiers(&text);" by:

        text = self
            .re_relay_log
            .replace_all(&text, |found: &regex::Captures<'_>| match (found.get(1), found.get(2)) {
                (Some(key), _) => format!("{}<client8>", key.as_str()),
                (_, Some(key)) => format!("{}<ms>", key.as_str()),
                (None, None) => String::new(),
            })
            .into_owned();
        text = self.identifiers(&text);

4. Module doc (first paragraph, the "Masked:" list), after "the encrypted body of a web push request (its length stays).": add " In the relay's log lines, the 8-hex phone id prefix after client= and phone:, and the milliseconds of lived= and loop-p50=/loop-p99=/loop-max=."
5. mod tests, add (run, masks and json! are the helpers of that module's tests; use serde_json::json! if json is not imported):

    #[test]
    fn relay_log_phone_prefixes_and_durations_are_masked() {
        let events = vec![
            json!({"ev": "log", "line": "[relay] phone leg closed client=1a2b3c4d code=1000 reason= lived=5ms"}),
            json!({"ev": "log", "line": "[relay] sockets 30s phones=1 buffered desktop:7c1f3a52=0B phone:d8601a87=0B loop-p50=31.6ms loop-p99=32.3ms loop-max=34.2ms"}),
        ];
        let out = run(masks(), events);
        assert_eq!(out[0]["line"], "[relay] phone leg closed client=<client8> code=1000 reason= lived=<ms>");
        assert_eq!(
            out[1]["line"],
            "[relay] sockets 30s phones=1 buffered desktop:7c1f3a52=0B phone:<client8>=0B loop-p50=<ms> loop-p99=<ms> loop-max=<ms>"
        );
    }

Run time: slow_silent_desktop_swept_then_offline_window_closes_phones takes about 65 s per run (the 45 s offline window cannot be shortened); the twin binary runs it four times (about 4.5 minutes).
